## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical performance optimization skills in real-world scenarios: code splitting, lazy loading strategies, and integrating automated performance validation into CI/CD pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- Code splitting: dynamic imports and React.lazy for component-level separation
- Visibility-based loading: IntersectionObserver for on-demand component loading
- Performance budgets: bundle size limits and Core Web Vitals thresholds
- Lighthouse CI: automated performance validation in CI/CD
- Resource optimization: lazy loading for non-critical resources
- User experience: loading states and skeleton screens to prevent layout shifts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Dynamic import for analytics chart
const HeavyChart = React.lazy(() => import('./charts/HeavyChart'));

// Visibility gate wrapper
function useVisible(ref) {
  const [visible, setVisible] = React.useState(false);
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
      ([entry]) => setVisible(entry.isIntersecting),
      { threshold: 0.1 }
    );
    if (ref.current) observer.observe(ref.current);
    return () => observer.disconnect();
  }, [ref]);
  return visible;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests real-time DOM updates, patch sequencing, offline-first architecture, and Service Worker integration for a collaborative design application.

## Key Concepts
- Patch sequencing with buffering for out-of-order delivery
- WebSocket reconnection with exponential backoff
- Offline storage using IndexedDB for pending mutations
- Service Worker asset caching
- DOM-based rendering vs virtual DOM diffing approaches

## Code Example
```javascript
function applyPatch(state, patch) {
  // minimal patch applier; ensure seq consistency
  const { op, shapeId, data } = patch;
  switch (op) {
    case 'add':
      state.shapes[shapeId] = data;
      break;
    case 'update':
      Object.assign(state.shapes[shapeId], data);
      break;
    case 'delete':
      delete state.shapes[shapeId];
      break;
  }
  return state;
}
```

## Integration Points and Trade-offs

| Component | Integration Point | Trade-off |
|-----------|------------------|-----------|
| WebSocket | Delta stream subscription | Complexity vs real-time consistency |
| IndexedDB | Offline mutation queue | Storage limits vs offline capability |
| Service Worker | Asset caching | Stale assets vs offline access |
| DOM Rendering | Shape display | Simplicity vs performance at scale |

